In message #94-3-237 on Saturday, March 19, Chris Phoenix wrote:

> I thought you were claiming that we were safe in criticizing the law
> of noncontradiction because any alternative would flunk the
> usefulness-and-applicability test, which we use all the time.  If you
> weren't saying that usefulness protects noncontradiction, then my
> point is moot.  But if you were, this seems inconsistent with your
> statement that usefulness is a "lesser" criticism, to be used only to
