interested in being reasonable, you reason with them. If they are not
interested in being reasonable, you defend against and ignore them. If
they are not interested in being reasonable and they refuse to be
ignored, then you defend yourself against them vigorously and
craftily. But at that point we're talking about physical defense and
real evasive maneuvers, not arguments and refutations.

One of the nice things about being reasonable is that verbal arguments
are so much less destructive than shootouts, SWAT teams, and tanks. 

> Given how much we learn from experience while growing up, what
