Better yet, see Hume. Also, see Chomsky on built-in grammatical
structures, and the evidence about creole languages which backs him up
on this. (Oops! Cross-linked thread!)

Are you arguing for a tabula-rasa theory of the infant mind? You seem
too knowledgeable to be doing that, so I'm not quite sure what you are
getting at.

